1
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone who's broke, come to me.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,020
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,440
A lullaby of duty and human kindness

5
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,140
Just stop it!

6
00:01:58,180 --> 00:01:59,380
What the hell are you doing?

7
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,040
Didn't you hear me?

8
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,640
We got here first, so this spot is ours.

9
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,700
I'm telling you to go somewhere else.

10
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:06,240
What?

11
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:07,720
That's a lie.

12
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:15,500
We've been camping out
here for three days already.

13
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,700
You stepped away to the bathroom
around noon for just a moment,

14
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,280
Those old geezers hijacked it!

15
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:31,560
Those newspapers weren't trash?

16
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,360
They're saying all sorts of things.

17
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,300
Ryotsu!

18
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,480
Ueno Park is big,
so why don't you just go somewhere else?

19
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,120
Yeah, why are you so hung up on this spot?

20
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,700
I can only think you're
the ones harassing us.

21
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:49,240
Long before you were in diapers, I'd already
decided to hold my cherry blossom viewing here.

22
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,380
Nooo!

23
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:50,740
Us!

24
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:51,520
What?

25
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:55,140
Alright, it's impossible. Let's give
up on this spot and move somewhere else.

26
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,240
It's too late. Look!

27
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:05,236
The cherry blossom spots
have already been claimed.

28
00:03:05,286 --> 00:03:06,860
What's left is...

29
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,560
We're doing it here no matter what!

30
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:13,500
Absolutely block them!

31
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,040
Yeah!

32
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:18,020
If that's how you want it,
we have our own plans.

33
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:24,860
What are you thinking?

34
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,960
It's bound to be something scummy anyway.

35
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,400
Scum.

36
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,760
If we need to, get Borubō to back us up too.

37
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:37,520
Hold out here until those
disrespectful bastards clear out.

38
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,920
Senpai, you're going somewhere?

39
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,520
That's not enough sake and snacks.

40
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,180
I'll go pick some up nearby.

41
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:45,720
Nakagawa.

42
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:51,220
Looks like you really clashed
with that disrespectful crew again.

43
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:51,940
Senpai.

44
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,685
Akagawa wouldn't understand.

45
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:59,815
Those guys think that if they make a racket,
their selfish demands will get through.

46
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:01,080
That's why they're impossible to handle.

47
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,008
You know,

48
00:04:02,058 --> 00:04:05,960
they must've been spoiled
rotten by their parents.

49
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:08,760
I think that's a different matter, though.

50
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,000
We've arrived, senpai's family home.

51
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,140
Sake and snacks, and so on.

52
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:17,740
Is it really okay?
Doing that without permission?

53
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,440
It's nothing unusual, don't worry about it.

54
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,260
Senpai, the baby's crying.

55
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:24,440
Baby?

56
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:27,748
Whoa, pon-pon-popon,

57
00:04:27,798 --> 00:04:29,626
the rabbit goes hop,

58
00:04:29,676 --> 00:04:32,260
den-den-daiko-denpon

59
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:33,680
What are you doing, Dad!

60
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,460
What did you come here for?

61
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,896
Hey, never mind that. That baby,

62
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:42,080
Don't you touch Chiyoko
with your filthy hands!

63
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:43,607
Chiyoko, you mean...

64
00:04:43,657 --> 00:04:47,480
Why is Kinjiro's Chiyoko here?

65
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:52,000
The baby who was born to your senior's
younger brother recently, right?

66
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:58,660
For some lawyer's daughter's wedding,
they left her with us just for today.

67
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:07,240
What did Mom say? A regular customer asked for hanami bento,
so she'll be right back after delivering it.

68
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:13,320
You should've gone yourself, Dad, at least stood up for it.
Saying that now won't change anything.

69
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:17,540
Hey, you, wake up!

70
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,620
Shut up.

71
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:23,220
I'll be right back after delivering
the hanami bento to Mr. Sasaki's.

72
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:26,820
Watch Chiyoko for a bit, will you?

73
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:30,080
Chiyoko.

74
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:33,160
Right, we took her in from Kinjiro's place.

75
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,200
If you take her out and she catches a cold,
it'll be a real problem.

76
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,260
Thanks.

77
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:39,400
Grandma's going out, Chiyoko.

78
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,280
Bye-bye.

79
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,700
Up high, up high!

80
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:49,020
She was sleeping quietly. You didn't make her sick or something,
did you?

81
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:53,380
She feels warm... or maybe not.

82
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:55,060
Pull yourself together, Kankichi!

83
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,060
And you call yourself a police officer?

84
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:00,620
Maybe her diaper is wet?

85
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,460
It's all lukewarm and damp.

86
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,720
Kankichi, which way is up on this one?

87
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:11,060
Either way, just hand her over quickly!

88
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,800
Chiyoko's going to catch a cold, you idiot!

89
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,300
That's serious!

90
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:19,960
You must have done something like that before, right?
I've forgotten things from so long ago.

91
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:22,940
Besides, back in my day I never
wore my hair tied up like this!

92
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:29,020
That last one must've been way easier, right?
Don't give me so much trouble!

93
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:32,440
Idiot! Don't use foul
language in front of Chiyoko!

94
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:35,080
Who's the one using foul language

95
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,880
What? Hey, you just laughed, didn't you?

96
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:42,220
No, I was just thinking you two really
are father and daughter after all.

97
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:45,100
Someone like this is a parent? What?

98
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:55,940
Analog!

99
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,760
Damn it.

100
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,280
If you two don't get along,

101
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:06,220
Chiyoko-chan won't stop crying at this rate.

102
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,220
Can't be helped.

103
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,920
It's for Chiyoko's sake.

104
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:16,780
Let's call a truce and pretend to get along.

105
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,220
Hey, what?

106
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:22,360
We don't see eye to eye, Kankichi.

107
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,340
Grandpa and Grandpa Kankichi are the best of friends,
you know.

108
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,660
Hehehehehe.

109
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:35,420
You're treating me way differently
than I treated you when you were a brat!

110
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:41,920
Brats with attitude like you
don't learn unless you get smacked.

111
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:44,860
Who did you get that attitude from,
I wonder?

112
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,460
What?

113
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,200
You've got to treat little girls with care,
you know.

114
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,760
I'm serious, you old geezer.

115
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,500
Not too hot, not too cold.

116
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,400
Here, it's chow time, Chiyoko.

117
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:01,240
Geez, what a rough-looking old man.

118
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:04,620
There you go, your little meal's ready.

119
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,980
So it's not too cold, see?

120
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:09,380
Chiyoko's going to grow
up to be a real beauty.

121
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:14,740
Take the best of Kinjirō and Keigo-san,
and make her speak fluent English too.

122
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:17,820
Have her learn tea ceremony,
flower arranging, and volleyball too.

123
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,680
A proper young lady's education Chiyoko?

124
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,140
Mm.

125
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:22,120
Ahahaha!

126
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:22,660
Ow.

127
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:25,660
Is Grandpa's flower arranging fun, Chiyoko?

128
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,840
Back in the day,
he was a heavy drinker and a womanizer.

129
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:32,240
The man who was famous for his
short temper is now a total letdown.

130
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:33,660
She is his first grandchild, after all.

131
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,200
He dotes on her so much,
he wouldn't mind her in his eyes.

132
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:36,760
I bet.

133
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,560
Putting her in your eyes would hurt,
you know.

134
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:41,380
Don't you think Meigo-san is cute, senpai?

135
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:41,960
Yeah.

136
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,440
If she's raised being coddled like that...

137
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,240
There.

138
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,820
Got a problem with that?

139
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:51,780
Yeah, yeah,
just thinking about it gives me chills.

140
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:53,860
You're getting ahead of yourself, senpai.

141
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:56,580
They say a child's character is set for life,
don't they?

142
00:08:56,580 --> 00:09:00,720
We need to start now and firmly teach him that no means no,
or he'll be hopeless.

143
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,680
Hey, Kankichi,
what do you think you're doing?

144
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:09,380
Fine, but unlike Pops, I'm not soft.

145
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:10,340
Abu.

146
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:14,280
Senpai, you can't say that to an infant.
They won't understand.

147
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:16,580
I'm going to be strict with you, got it?

148
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,020
Waaah.

149
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:27,940
Kuu.

150
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,720
Sucking up at your age, you little brat.

151
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,540
S-so cute.

152
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,980
She's adorable, no question about it.

153
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,000
Did you have fun, Chiyoko?

154
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,040
She had fun, didn't she?

155
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:06,820
Damn it, to think I, of all people, got beaten by a baby.
How pathetic.

156
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,520
You should stop wasting your effort, Senpai.

157
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:13,660
Isn't it said that you should
give in to whatever's cute?

158
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,340
Well then, I should be getting
back to the police box now.

159
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,560
If you're going to say that, it's
"give in to whoever's stronger."

160
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,880
Sorry for calling you away
while you were on duty.

161
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:29,260
You should come to the
cherry blossom viewing too.

162
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:31,400
I'll be over there from five o'clock.

163
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,700
Yes, but Senpai, will you be all right?

164
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,160
Leaving Dad alone with her?

165
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:39,820
Surely Mom will be back by then,
no matter what.

166
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,980
Listen to me, dear.

167
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:45,540
He said it was for emergencies,

168
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:47,420
the secret savings I'd been stashing away

169
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:49,520
and now he says he blew
it all on the horses.

170
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:52,820
That sounds like a story I've heard before.

171
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,560
Now that you mention it, that's my money!

172
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:59,900
What I spend it on is none of your business!

173
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,680
You'd better just apologize honestly.

174
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,240
What about your promise to the grandkid?

175
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,020
Chiyoko?

176
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:11,140
I promised my granddaughter
I'd buy her a bicycle.

177
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,540
Hey, you two should talk things
over properly as a married couple.

178
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,700
Well then, I'd better be going.

179
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:17,920
That's not all, Yone-san.

180
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,320
Is there something else?

181
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:21,160
Phew.

182
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:38,240
The girls over there seem to be having fun.

183
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:40,040
That Volvo guy is taking his time, isn't he.

184
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,100
It's useless even if you harass us.

185
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:44,880
We're not moving from here, no matter what.

186
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,180
Hey, Komachi.

187
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,800
What's that?

188
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:59,220
The cherry blossoms will scatter before the hanami party,
damn it!

189
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:01,800
Pardon me.

190
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,620
Damn it, I miscalculated the wind.

191
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,640
Is everyone all right?

192
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,580
Are you the one who's okay?

193
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:15,560
Is the enemy still
illegally occupying the spot?

194
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:17,360
Are you an idiot or what?

195
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,900
Don't stand behind me.

196
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:36,200
They're blooming
beautifully again this year.

197
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:40,120
Hey there, ladies,
shall we have you clear that spot?

198
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,880
What's Mom doing?

199
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,500
Mom doesn't have a cell phone?

200
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,040
As if she'd have something like that!

201
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:03,600
She can't even use the TV remote properly,
that's what they say.

202
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,100
Right, isn't it, Chiyoko?

203
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:07,900
She said she'd be right back, didn't she?

204
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,640
Now that you mention it,
it's been two or three hours already.

205
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,680
Kankichi, you've got work to do, don't you?

206
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,020
I'll watch Chiyoko, so you can go.

207
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:20,900
I can't just leave, not with Dad alone.
It's worrying!

208
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:24,940
Mom...

209
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,160
Just a moment, please.

210
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:28,560
To Dad...

211
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:30,060
Even the pines of Sendagi...

212
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:35,140
Matsu-san, long time no see, chu.

213
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:37,460
Anyway,

214
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:38,660
Honestly.

215
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,020
That's a cruel thing to say.

216
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,320
Not again.

217
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,500
Well, that's a bit inconvenient.

218
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,560
I'd love to come over, but

219
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,380
I'm really sorry.

220
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,900
Matsu from Sendagi?

221
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,440
An old acquaintance.

222
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:08,000
Years ago, he saved my life, so I owe him.

223
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,120
He saved your life?

224
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:13,860
That was when Kankichi
was about Chiyoko's age.

225
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:18,820
I was a cocky kid, and over something trivial
I got into a fight with some street punks.

226
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,640
Come on, go for it!

227
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,520
Shut up!

228
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,440
What's your name?

229
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,220
That was Matsu of Sendagi.

230
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,100
I've never heard that story before.

231
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,120
It would only worry you.

232
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,860
I never told Yone, either.

233
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:03,800
And this Matsu of Sendagi is now...

234
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:06,080
apparently caught up in
some dangerous business.

235
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,100
Dangerous business?

236
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,380
So that earlier call was

237
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:23,800
a call asking the old man for help?

238
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:27,360
Is that alright?
He saved your life, didn't he?

239
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:29,920
If you go, you won't get off easy.

240
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,500
Even your cute grandchild's face,

241
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:34,460
you might never get to see it again.

242
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,180
There's no way I can go.

243
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,040
Yeah, at our age,

244
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,320
there's no need to jump
into the fire on purpose.

245
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:43,640
Anyway, it's the debt of
gratitude I owed since I was a kid.

246
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:47,839
That's a story from long, long ago.

247
00:15:47,889 --> 00:15:49,400
It's past the statute of limitations.

248
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:54,060
What? When did you become such a noble man?

249
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:58,080
Hey, that's unfair!
You just said yourself you weren't going!

250
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:02,600
H-hey, I finally got comfy turning over,
and now you've gone and woken me up!

251
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,121
Hey,

252
00:16:07,171 --> 00:16:11,800
Where'd you come from carrying that thing?

253
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:17,820
Weigh duty against human feeling, and duty comes out heavier.
That's a man's world.

254
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:23,160
Chiyoko, forgive your foolish grandpa.

255
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:27,140
I wanted to see you in your bridal dress.

256
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:31,500
Seriously, Dad!

257
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:33,400
Chiyoko, time!

258
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:34,600
Dad!

259
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:36,340
Chiyoko, time!

260
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:39,160
Hey! Wait up, Dad!

261
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:42,600
What's wrong?

262
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:45,220
Are you all right?

263
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:46,660
Don't worry.

264
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:51,480
I got all worked up,
so my blood's suddenly rushing.

265
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:56,660
Seeing Chiyoko's face,
my firm resolve is starting to waver.

266
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:04,560
Damn it, don't you dare stop me, Kankichi!

267
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,480
Wait a minute, old man.

268
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:09,820
What are you doing?

269
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:13,880
I'll go. So I just have to rescue
that Matsu from Sendagi, right?

270
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,460
Kankichi, this has nothing to do with you.

271
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,500
A debt owed to a father
is a debt the son inherits.

272
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:23,000
Kankichi, don't worry.

273
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,500
This way.

274
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:37,700
Boss, those women aren't ordinary.

275
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:40,720
Hold the line at all costs! We will win!

276
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,500
Let's talk it out! Talk it out!

277
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:46,080
Here we go! Formation X!

278
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:47,880
Look out, Boss!

279
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:51,380
Right, under cover of the dirt tactic, we'll go in too!
Let's move!

280
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:56,211
Senpai!
Things have gotten totally out of hand,

281
00:17:56,261 --> 00:18:00,020
we can't seem to settle
this without you, Senpai!

282
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,500
Well, I've got some errands of my own.

283
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:05,600
What? You can't come?
That's not fair, Senpai!

284
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:09,540
I'll come,
so hold on a little longer on your own.

285
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,300
Go on, Kankichi.

286
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:15,640
You have an important job,
protecting the citizens.

287
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:18,900
We can't let you die uselessly
in someone else's place.

288
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,780
Is the other side really that dangerous?

289
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:25,160
If even Matsu of Sendagi needs help,

290
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,500
it must be serious, right?

291
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:34,600
Chiyoko, I'm counting on you.

292
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,180
Take care, Kankichi.

293
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:39,200
Senpai, senpai, please come quickly!

294
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,500
Damn it, what are we supposed to do?

295
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:45,160
Sorry, I'm so late.

296
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,780
I got caught up in a married couple's fight.

297
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,500
Chiyoko?

298
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:50,600
You.

299
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:54,680
Where on earth did he go, carrying Chiyoko?

300
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:56,980
Wait a minute, Dad.

301
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:01,160
What about Mom?
You're going to leave her behind alone?

302
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:02,320
Yone.

303
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:06,100
You've caused her nothing but hardship,
and now you're selfishly going off ahead?

304
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:09,880
Yone will understand. She's sure to.

305
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,000
I understand.

306
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:14,120
I have to go now.

307
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:17,920
She's stuck by a fool like
me for all these years.

308
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:21,800
She'll laugh and forgive
even my last selfish whim.

309
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:25,380
Don't be ridiculous.
Even if Mom forgives me, I won't.

310
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:29,860
If I go off alone like this, I'll never
forgive myself for the rest of my life.

311
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,120
Chiyo-kun,
take good care of Dad and Mom, okay?

312
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:36,640
Dad, your fly's open.

313
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:36,940
What?

314
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:38,500
Hey, Kankichi!

315
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:40,880
It's to the right.

316
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:51,140
You, with a family of your own,
can't take my place.

317
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,840
Dad, just worry about Chiyo-kun.

318
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:55,880
Really?

319
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:58,820
Aren't your underlings waiting for you?

320
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:02,520
You've got your own fight,
haven't you, Kankichi?

321
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,740
Eeeeeh?

322
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,500
It's bad!

323
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,840
Ryotsu! SOS!

324
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,280
Uh...

325
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:30,460
Sorry, Honda, forgive me, Volvo, Sagonji. This is the one
great act of filial devotion a lone old man like me can offer.

326
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:32,580
Mm.

327
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:37,940
Let's hurry up and go sort this out, Pop.

328
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:39,700
Kankichi.

329
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,600
Ueno Park is a bloodbath for men.

330
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,540
Ueno? Cherry blossoms?

331
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,720
Is this Ueno Park?

332
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,620
What a mess.

333
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,820
And I thought we'd be drinking
under the cherry blossoms.

334
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,220
How pathetic.

335
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:09,000
Matsu!

336
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:11,300
Ginji.

337
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:12,860
You came, then?

338
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:15,840
I'll properly repay the old debt I owe you.

339
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:18,320
Who's the opponent?

340
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,940
This man is the last of the Sendagi line.

341
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:30,740
Senpai, you really did come after all.

342
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:31,800
Honda

343
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:35,580
Tell those guys it's against the rules.

344
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:38,020
We can't handle this with restraint tactics.

345
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:40,340
You boys did a good job too.

346
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,680
No choice.

347
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,700
Eeeeeeh!

348
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,060
Matsu of Sendagi's enemy.

349
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:47,980
That means they're our enemy too.

350
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:55,160
You two are so persistent.

351
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,140
Why don't you just give up already?

352
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:02,040
The dangerous business about my
life-saver getting caught up in it

353
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:03,920
is that what this is about?

354
00:22:08,540 --> 00:22:11,620
Well, at least we both escaped with our lives,
so that's good, isn't it?

355
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:18,040
Massa, this is my son Kankichi,
and this is my first grandchild, Chiyoko.

356
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:19,640
Please remember us from now on.

357
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,260
I see.

358
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:22,160
Don't mess with me.

359
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:25,400
Look, you've startled Chiyoko!

360
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:28,440
Baby.

361
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,320
Really.

362
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:34,080
She's so cute. Whose baby is she?

363
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,160
No way.

364
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:38,140
No, she's the baby of my
younger brother Kinjirō.

365
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:40,060
Yeah, she's adorable, isn't she?

366
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:41,300
What's that supposed to mean?

367
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:42,960
Can I hold her?

368
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:43,460
Mm-hmm.

369
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:51,200
Well, I suppose I can't say no. For Chiyoko's sake,
I'll let you join us for cherry blossom viewing here.

370
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:56,020
Cheers!

371
00:22:56,540 --> 00:22:58,140
Haah.

372
00:22:58,140 --> 00:23:05,920
Lucky you, Chiyeko,
being held by a pretty lady.

373
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:11,600
Really? Grandpa's a tatami maker?

374
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:16,900
You bet. Leave it to me,
and I'll re-tatami the White House in a day.

375
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:17,480
Really?

376
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:19,980
If the White House had tatami mats, that is.

377
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:22,840
Well, days like this happen.

378
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:23,920
You!

379
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:30,460
Thank goodness Chiyoko's safe.
You had me worried sick!

380
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:32,820
When I got back, Chiyoko was gone,
and so was everyone else.

381
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:37,300
The police box contacted us,
so I called Senpai's cell phone,

382
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:41,400
but it didn't connect. So I thought maybe you'd be here,
and brought you along.

383
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:47,780
Honestly, dragging a baby
around must have worn you out

384
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,520
Honestly, yes.

385
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:50,460
Hand-knitted.

386
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:55,420
I just wanted to show Chiyoko her
first cherry blossoms in her life.

387
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:24,560
I walked, looking back on
the day after the rain stopped,

388
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:27,180
holding Mom's hand.

389
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:34,420
That strange feeling I had back then,

390
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:39,600
so on the tiles of the arcade street,

391
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:45,280
I tried walking only on the black ones.

392
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

393
00:24:54,620 --> 00:25:01,000
Pompous-faced politicians,
and aunties who are a thorn in your side,

394
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:06,580
go on, turn that corner over there.

395
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:11,700
You can meet everyone, everyone!

396
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:16,400
Over there, there's a turtle (Kameari)!

397
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:19,760
Well, I'm sure there's a turtle (Kameari)!

398
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,880
Come on, everyone, come to our town!

399
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

400
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:33,220
Why did I ever end up with such a crybaby?

401
00:25:33,220 --> 00:25:36,720
And today of all days,
the Chief has to sit in the seat of honor.

402
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:38,660
Nakagawa's being uncooperative, too.

403
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:40,540
Terai's acting suspicious, too.

404
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:44,740
We have to erase the graffiti quickly,
or something terrible will happen!

405
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:48,240
Next time, erase the graffiti! Thanks!

406
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:50,900
Over there is Kameari!

407
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:54,640
Well, it's surely Kameari!

408
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:59,260
Come on, everyone, come to our town!

409
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:00,840
Thank you!

